          Chapter one
        </span>
      

      
        <h2>
          The surface is the scorecard.<br>
It is not the story.
        </h2>
      

      
        <div class="lvg-truth-scorecard__two">

          
            <div>
              <p>A breakout. A dark spot that has outlasted the spot that made it. A dull patch. A pore you can see in the mirror at arm's length. These are real. Nothing here is going to tell you they do not matter, or that the grown-up response is to stop minding them. They matter enough that most of this brand exists to address them.</p>
            </div>
          

          
            <div>
              <p>But every one of them is an endpoint. It is what a process underneath the surface looks like after it has already happened — and after years of how the skin has been treated. Take each endpoint as an isolated enemy and you spend your life correcting manifestations one at a time.</p><p>Which is, not at all coincidentally, the exact routine the previous part of this story described.</p>
            </div>
          

        </div>
      

    </article>
